- Remembered data is bounded: lists/maps that grow with play (logs, queues, remembered changes) have a configured maximum (drop the oldest), stored per chunk/player key so one lookup never scans everything.
- Every limit is a config.yml setting with a SAFE default (radius 4 chunks / 16 blocks, per-tick 64 or less, mob copying off). The owner may raise it: HONOUR the saved value (log one warning naming the likely cost when it is above the recommended maximum; never clamp it silently, only to crash-safe bounds such as >= 1). Big values must still work: spread the work over ticks with NxPerf.queue / NxPerf.grant so a large radius runs slower instead of never running. If the request asks for unbounded work ("every chunk", "infinite", "all entities every tick"), build it bounded by these settings, default them safely and say so in modbuilder.json "limitations".
