// Cyrus Config and Stats Studio: ConfigSpec v1, the ONE typed model of a mod's tunable settings (mob stats, weapon
// stats, ability cooldowns, shop prices, boss phases, quest rewards, arena timers...). GAME-NEUTRAL: a param is a
// typed value at a dotted key with limits, units and how a change takes effect; per-game exporters (./exporters.ts)
// say how a file is written and reloaded. The designers' params (lib/cyrus/designer) convert into this model
// (./designer.ts), imported mods get an inferred spec (./infer.ts), AI-built mods declare one (assets/config/schema.json).
// Pure + client-safe. Zod in code, `configSpecJsonSchema()` is the portable contract. Rule failures come back as
// structured issues { path, code, message }, never a thrown error.
// LIMITS (owner rule 2026-10-12, D-62 "warn, don't block"; lib/cyrus/limits): `min`/`max` are the RECOMMENDED range
// (outside it the editor warns and still saves, generated loaders log once and apply the value), `warnMin`/`warnMax`
// start the danger tier (one confirm), `hardMin`/`hardMax` are crash-safe bounds only (the one thing still refused /
// clamped), `safe` is the balanced band inside the recommended range, `impact` says what a bigger value costs.
